{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design", "label": "Worktree Rototill: Detect-and-Defer Design Spec", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_detect_and_defer", "label": "Detect-and-Defer Worktree Strategy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defer to native harness worktree systems when they exist and only fill the gap where native support is absent, eliminating the duplication, conflict, and phantom-state failure modes of superpowers' opinionated worktree management."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_detect_state_not_platform", "label": "Detect State, Not Platform (GIT_DIR != GIT_COMMON)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GIT_DIR != GIT_COMMON is a stable git primitive (since git 2.5, 2015) that detects 'am I already in a worktree?' universally across all harnesses with zero maintenance as new harnesses appear, instead of sniffing environment variables to identify the harness."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_declarative_intent_prescriptive_fallback", "label": "Declarative Intent, Prescriptive Fallback", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The skill should describe the goal and defer to native tools, prescribing concrete git commands only as a fallback; TDD proved agents anchor on Step 1b's concrete commands when Step 1a is too vague, so explicit tool naming (EnterWorktree, WorktreeCreate, /worktree, --worktree) plus a consent-authorization bridge were required to make native-tool preference reliable (2/6 to 50/50 pass rate)."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_provenance_based_ownership", "label": "Provenance-Based Worktree Ownership", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Whoever creates the worktree owns its cleanup: worktrees under .worktrees/ or worktrees/ are superpowers-owned and it cleans them; anything else (.claude/worktrees/, ~/.codex/worktrees/, .gemini/worktrees/, user-global paths) belongs to the harness or user and is left alone."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_step_1a_native_tools", "label": "Step 1a: Native Worktree Tools (preferred)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Names native worktree tools explicitly so the decision becomes a factual tool-list lookup rather than interpretation; frames the user's Step 0 consent as the authorization the tool's guardrail requires (tool descriptions override skill instructions, Claude Code #29950), and a Red Flag entry names the anti-pattern of using git worktree add when a native tool exists."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_step_1b_git_fallback", "label": "Step 1b: Git Worktree Fallback", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Manual git worktree add is used only when no native tool is available, with directory selection from the agent instruction file or existing .worktrees/ directory, git check-ignore safety verification, hooks symlinking from the main repo (PR #965), and a sandbox permission-error fallback to work in place."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_opt_in_consent", "label": "Opt-In Worktree Consent (Step 0.5)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolves issue #991 by making worktree creation opt-in rather than mandatory; the consent prompt protects the user's current branch and is skipped entirely when Step 0 already detects existing isolation."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_bug_fixes", "label": "Bundled Bug Fixes (#940, #999, #238)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Finishing-skill fixes: #940 removes contradictory worktree-cleanup prose so cleanup runs only for Options 1 and 4; #999 reorders to merge, verify tests, remove worktree, delete branch (deleting the branch first fails because the worktree still references it, and removing the worktree first risks losing changes if the merge fails); #238 adds a CWD guard that cds to the main repo root before git worktree remove. Cleanup is additionally followed by git worktree prune as a self-healing step against stale registrations (PR #1072)."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_detect_and_defer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_detect_state_not_platform", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_detect_and_defer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_declarative_intent_prescriptive_fallback", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_detect_and_defer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_provenance_based_ownership", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_detect_and_defer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_declarative_intent_prescriptive_fallback", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_step_1a_native_tools", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-06-worktree-rototill-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_step_1a_native_tools", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_04_06_worktree_rototill_design_step_1b_git_fallbac